abstract: >-
  EpiCalc is a free, mobile-friendly, open-source web application for
  epidemiology metrics, epidemic simulation, and biostatistics. Features
  include risk metrics (RR, OR, ARR, NNT), disease frequency measures
  (attack rate, CFR, mortality rates), vaccine efficacy and herd immunity
  threshold, burden of disease (DALYs, YLL, YLD), screening test
  performance (sensitivity, specificity, PPV, NPV, likelihood ratios), an
  interactive SIR/SEIR epidemic simulator with real-time R0
  visualization, and a biostatistics calculator (sample size, Z-test,
  t-test, chi-square, ANOVA). The app runs entirely client-side as an
  installable, offline-capable Progressive Web App, with no data
  collection, and is optimized for low-bandwidth (2G/3G) environments.
